-- title:
--   Transport of the base full level along a rigidification
-- statement:
--   The data are organised in blocks, each of which is named below; no hypothesis is passed over, and where a block has many clauses its content is summarised impersonally.
--
--   **Numerical data.** Primes $r$, $\bar r$ and a nonzero natural number $N$, with $\bar r\neq r$ (`hrr`), $r\nmid N$ (`hrN`), $\bar r\nmid N$ (`hrbarN`) and $N$ squarefree (`hN`).
--
--   **Coefficients.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi$ an irreducible element, $\mathcal O$ is $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), $\mathcal O/\pi$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Further, $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, which is $\pi$-adically complete (`hOnr_complete`), has $\pi O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ maximal (`hOnr_max`), is such that every element satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`) and every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). The homomorphism $vdet:GL_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$, written multiplicatively, satisfies `hvdet`: $vdet(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$, i.e. $vdet$ is the $\pi$-valuation of the determinant.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion side and coarse moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies above $r$ or $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`); a scheme $\mathcal X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, a point map `pt` on fake elliptic curves (in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve Λ N S`: a relative group scheme over $S$ with two-dimensional fibres, an abelian-scheme property bundle, a $\Lambda$-action with trace condition and a level-$N$ subscheme), and `h𝒳 : IsCoarseModuli Λ N 𝒳 f pt` (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property).
--
--   **Full level $n$ and fine moduli.** A natural number $n$ with $3\le n$, $r\nmid n$, $\bar r\nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N)=1$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `ptF` on pairs (fake elliptic curve, full level-$n$ structure) and `hM : IsFineModuli` (four clauses: isomorphism invariance, base change, surjectivity and injectivity of `ptF`); a group $G$ with $\rho:G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ and labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ satisfying `hρ : IsLevelTwistAction` (the automorphisms are over the base, they realise twisting of the level structure by $\chi(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative and bijective modulo $n\Lambda$). Here a full level-$n$ structure on $E$ is a section $P$ of $E.f$ killed by $n$, whose $\Lambda$-orbit exhausts the geometric $n$-torsion and whose annihilator in $\Lambda$ is $n\Lambda$.
--
--   **Degeneracy and Hecke data.** A morphism $p:M\to\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the point maps (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `ptT` on pairs carrying an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup and `h𝒴 : IsCoarseModuliT`, together with two morphisms $d_0,d_1:\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) realising on points the forgetting of the $\ell$-structure (`hd₀`) and the quotient by it (`hd₁`, via `IsLevelIsogeny`). Morphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}:\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ ramified exactly at the places above $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`); an adelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) whose meet order is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ containing $r$ (`hv`); the subgroup $\Gamma^t$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times$ characterised by `hΓt` as the group of units of $R_1$ away from $v$; for each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ elements $s_\ell$ and adelic units $s_{f,\ell}$ subject to `hs` (four clauses: $s_{f,\ell}$ equals $s_\ell$ at all places not above $r$ and is $1$ at places above $r$, the product of the diagonal image of $\ell$ with $s_{f,\ell}^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set, respectively the prime Hecke set, of the meet order according as $\ell\mid N$ or not, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$), with $\Gamma^t_\ell=\Gamma^t\cap s_\ell\Gamma^t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Integral coordinates.** The hypothesis `hΛℤ` that every integer lies in $\Lambda$, and `hcoord : IsOrderCoord Λ r coord` for a map $coord:\Lambda\to W(\mathbb F_{r^2})^2$ (six clauses: additivity, normalisation at $1$, the $\varpi$-twisted multiplication rule, injectivity, $r$-adic density, and the trace formula).
--
--   **The base object over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$.** A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ for $A_0$, with `hA₀` identifying the formal group of $A_0$ with $X_0$ compatibly with $coord$; families $e,e'$ of endomorphisms of $A_0.A$ indexed by $\Gamma^t$ with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees `deg`. The conditions on this family, summarised here, are: `hE1` ($e\gamma,e'\gamma$ form an $r^{\deg\gamma}$-isogeny pair and $e\gamma$ preserves the level-$N$ structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity up to powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (scalars in $\Gamma^t$ act by multiplication up to powers of $r$), `hE1'` (conversely, if $e\gamma$ is a multiplication up to a power of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring map from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in GL_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on $\theta_0$ by a centraliser element whose image is $r^{k_\gamma}\,g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (for every full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ a labelling $\Gamma^t\to\Lambda$ of the action of $e\gamma$, multiplicative and normalised modulo $n\Lambda$), `hE4` (every level-preserving $r^d$-isogeny pair of a fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ comes, up to multiplications by powers of $r$, from some $e\gamma$), and the block `hE5a`–`hE5e` for a suborder $R_2\le R_1$ with $r$-power denominators (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`) and a family $\hat e$ indexed by $R_2$ (`hê`): additivity, $\Lambda$-equivariance and level preservation, multiplicativity and normalisation, the norm relation $\hat e(\bar x)\circ\hat e(x)=[\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$, compatibility of $\hat e$ with $e$ on scalar multiples of elements of $\Gamma^t$, and a joint matching of $e$ and $\hat e$ with $\iota_0$ on formal coordinates.
--
--   **The Drinfeld side.** A ring map $\iota:W(\mathbb F_{r^2})\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a map $\eta$ from rigidified objects to points of $MD$ subject to `hη` (three clauses: on admissible rigidified objects, equality of $\eta$-values is equivalence of rigidifications; naturality under base change; and local-on-the-base surjectivity of $\eta$); an injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\varpi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the precise bounded-denominator sense of `hE₀`. Then the block `eD`, `hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD`: a natural bijection between the functor of $MD$-points over $\pi$-nilpotent Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras and the product of $\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O}(O^{\mathrm{nr}},-)$ with Drinfeld's functor $\Omega$, compatible with the first projection, carrying the $GL_2(K_0)$-action on $MD$-points to the twisted action on $\Omega$-data, carrying $\pi$-translation to the Frobenius twist of the first leg, and with $\pi$-translates always existing.
--
--   **Comparison data.** A ring map $\kappa:O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/r$ with `hκ`; a natural number $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$. The Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$: a fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$, morphisms $a_w,a_w',b_w,b_w'$ over the base with $k_w$, such that $(a_w,a_w')$ realises the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), $(b_w,b_w')$ is an $r^{k_w}$-isogeny pair (`hBSw`) with $b_w$ level-preserving (`hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw` matching both the $e\gamma$ and the composite of $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ on formal coordinates with $\iota_0(\gamma)$ and $\iota_0(\bar w)$ conjugated by one and the same $g$, up to powers of $r$.
--
--   **The comparison map $\Xi$ and the element $g_0$.** A map $\Xi$ sending a rigidified curve over a $\pi$-nilpotent Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with leg $\psi$ to a $G$-point of $MD$, subject to `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ the leg of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality under pullback of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves compatible up to powers of $r$) and `hΞdef` (over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, $\Xi$ is computed by $\eta$ applied to an admissible rigidified object obtained by rigidified transport along $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$ with exponent $j\le 1$, the leg being the $(-j)$-th Frobenius twist of $\psi$); finally $g_0\in GL_2(K_0)$ with `heqΓ` ($\Xi$ of two rigidifications of the same curve that differ by translation by $e\gamma$ differ by the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$ for some $c\in\mathbb Z$) and `heqW` (the analogous statement for the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ and $\iota_0(\bar w)$).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $\psi^{\circ}=\psi\circ Fr^{-v_\pi(\det g_0)}$ for the Frobenius twist of $\psi$ by $-\mathrm{toAdd}(vdet\,g_0)$. The conclusion is a conjunction of two assertions, both quantified over every Noetherian commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$, and every rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ along $\psi^{\circ}$ — that is, a fake elliptic curve $\varrho.E_b$ over $B/\pi$ with $\varrho.g_b:\varrho.E_b.A\to E.A$ exhibiting it as the reduction of $E$, a fake elliptic curve $\varrho.A_b$ over $B/\pi$ with $\varrho.g_A:\varrho.A_b.A\to A_0.A$ exhibiting it as the pullback of $A_0$ along the residue leg of $\psi^{\circ}$, and a level-preserving $r^{\varrho.d}$-isogeny pair $\varrho.\varphi:\varrho.E_b.A\to\varrho.A_b.A$, $\varrho.\varphi':\varrho.A_b.A\to\varrho.E_b.A$.
--
--   First, existence: there is a full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $E$ and a morphism $Q:\operatorname{Spec}(B/\pi B)\to\varrho.A_b.A$ such that $Q$ followed by $\varrho.A_b.f$ is the identity of $\operatorname{Spec}(B/\pi B)$; $Q$ followed by $\varrho.g_A$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue leg $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi\to B/\pi$ attached to $\psi^{\circ}$ followed by the section underlying $P_0$; and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient map $B\to B/\pi B$ followed by the section underlying $P_n$ equals $Q$ followed by $\varrho.\varphi'$ followed by $\varrho.g_b$.
--
--   Second, uniqueness: if $P_n$ and $P_n'$ are full level-$n$ structures on $E$ each satisfying the displayed condition (with its own auxiliary morphism $Q$), then the underlying sections agree, $P_n.P=P_n'.P$.
--
--   This is the level-structure step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison for moduli of fake elliptic curves: it transports the chosen full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on the base object $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$ through a rigidification to a full level-$n$ structure on an arbitrary fake elliptic curve over a $\pi$-nilpotent Noetherian base, and shows the transported structure is determined by its defining property. It is used in the uniqueness statement for rigidified pairs, `evenRigidifiedPair_unique_of_rigidifiedToG_of_forall_isIdempotentElem_of_isUnit_two`.
